# Browser Screenshot Policy

Do NOT take browser screenshots after every code change. Screenshots are expensive and slow.

## When to screenshot

- Debugging a **visual bug** the user reported (with a screenshot or description)
- The user explicitly asks you to verify something visually
- Final verification after a **large batch of changes** (not after each individual edit)

## When NOT to screenshot

- After routine CSS/component edits — trust the compiler and linter
- After each file save — batch changes first, verify once at the end if needed
- To confirm HMR picked up a change — it almost always does
- After navigation — the browser snapshot from `browser_navigate` already confirms the page loaded

## Preferred workflow

1. Make all code changes
2. Run `tsc --noEmit` and `ReadLints` to verify correctness
3. Only screenshot if there's a specific visual concern
